{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cosmopolitan is an international fashion magazine for women.","title":"Cosmopolitan (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Formerly titled The Cosmopolitan, the magazine was first published in 1886 in the United States as a family magazine; it was later transformed into a literary magazine and eventually became a women's magazine since 1965.","title":"Cosmopolitan (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Often referred to as Cosmo, its content as of 2011 includes articles on relationships, sex, health, careers, self-improvement, celebrities, fashion, and beauty.","title":"Cosmopolitan (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Published by Hearst Corporation, "Cosmopolitan" has 64 international editions, is printed in 35 languages, and is distributed in more than 110 countries.","title":"Cosmopolitan (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Skinny House in Mamaroneck, New York was built in 1932 by African-American carpenter and building contractor Nathan Thomas Seely on an extremely narrow lot of donated land after he lost his home to foreclosure and his company to bankruptcy during the early years of the Great Depression.","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The 10 ft wide house has 3 stories and was built on a 12.5 ft wide plot of land sold to him by his neighbor, to whom he had earlier sold a larger plot of land.","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The house was constructed entirely from salvaged materials.","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The New York State Board for Historic Preservation noted “its efficient and beautiful design, careful engineering, and effective interior plan.","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Challenged by a narrow lot and minimal financial means, Seely created a house that demonstrated both his ingenuity and the desire to provide, above all else, housing for his family.”","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Westchester County Historical Society said “its professional construction and ingenious design are a testimony to the dedication of a prominent black contractor to build a solid, functional, and delightful home.","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It represents both black enterprise and good neighborliness, and is architecturally significant as a symbol of American ingenuity and craftsmanship.”","title":"Skinny House (Mamaroneck, New York)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"African-American bookstores, also known as black bookstores, are bookstores owned and operated by African Americans.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" These stores often, although not always, specialize in works by and about African Americans and their target customers are often African Americans.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Although they are a variety of African-American business, African American bookstores have often been closely tied to radical political movements including Marxism, Black Power, and pan-Africanism.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":"The first documented African-American bookstore was established by the abolitionist David Ruggles in 1834.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" One of the earliest African-American bookstores to achieve national prominence was Lewis Michaux's National Memorial African Bookstore, which operated in Harlem from the early 1930s to the middle of the 1970s.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Michaux's store doubled as a meeting place for black activists, including most famously Malcolm X.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The Black Power movement embraced black-owned bookstores in the 1960s and '70s as vehicles for promoting their ideology and creating radical political spaces in black communities across the United States.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" By the 1990s, African-American bookstores earned significant attention from more politically moderate and business oriented media outlets such as the magazine Black Enterprise.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" In the 2000s and 2010s, however, as independent bookstores of all kinds declined and bookstores chains and Amazon increasingly sold black-authored books, the number of African-American bookstores declined rapidly, dropping from over 250 to just over 70.","title":"African-American bookstores"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rose Catherine Pinkney (born 1964) is an American television development executive.","title":"Rose Catherine Pinkney"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She was hired as the VP Development and Original Programming for TV Land in 2012.","title":"Rose Catherine Pinkney"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Pinkney has previously served as Director of Programming at Twentieth Century Fox Television, Senior Vice President of Comedy Development at Paramount Pictures Television and executive vice president of programming and production at TV One.","title":"Rose Catherine Pinkney"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" She most recently served as the head of the television arm of Laurence Fishburne's production company, Cinema Gypsy.","title":"Rose Catherine Pinkney"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Among Pinkney's accolades are Network Journal's 25 Most Influential Black Women in Business, Cable World's Top 50 Women in Cable and Black Enterprise's Top 50 Entertainment Executives.","title":"Rose Catherine Pinkney"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Our World with Black Enterprise is a weekly television show currently hosted by Paul Brunson, and, during its first season, Marc Lamont Hill which is produced by Black Enterprise, Inc. It airs on Saturday and Sunday across a range of local television stations and focuses on various issues of interest to the urban (i.e. Black) general and upwardly mobile community.","title":"Our World with Black Enterprise"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Black Enterprise Business Report is a weekly television show produced by Black Enterprise, Inc..","title":"Black Enterprise Business Report"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It airs across a range of United States local television stations on varying times and days of the week.","title":"Black Enterprise Business Report"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Black Enterprise also produces another show titled "Our World with Black Enterprise".","title":"Black Enterprise Business Report"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: media companies
